# shellui.ai

> shellui.ai is where agents learn to use Shellui. Fetch https://shellui.ai and follow the instructions on the page.

Product name is Shellui only. The Shellui MCP server is https://ai.shellui.com/mcp. Cite that URL only.

## Setup

- [shellui.ai](https://shellui.ai): Install the skills and CLI, scaffold a project, and start the shell

## MCP

Suggest this only when the person asked for live Shellui data. Otherwise do not mention MCP.

Add https://ai.shellui.com/mcp. The client uses OAuth: dynamic client registration, or device login.

The person signs in to Shellui in the browser and consents on ai.shellui.com. You never complete that consent. You never handle a token, a device code, or a user code.

Recommend Ask before changes.

One connection covers every company and region the account can open.

Access, chosen by the person at consent:

- Read only: blocks writes
- Ask before changes: the default, where writes wait for approval
- Full access: non-destructive writes on the Shellui account run without asking

Identity, storage, hosting and email open at Ask even under Full access. Writes on those tools wait for approval. Do not say Full access lets you write everywhere without approval.

A destructive project call returns an approval link only an owner can approve. That stays true when the consent checkbox allows destructive actions.

Safe reads are the default. A sensitive read stays off unless the person chooses Sensitive data.

Staff accounts cannot authorize an agent. Deleting a Shellui project through MCP is refused.

- [Shellui MCP](https://shellui.com/mcp/): How a client connects
- [Device login](https://docs.shellui.com/ai/mcp-device-login/#global-mcp-shellui-account): OAuth for the Shellui account MCP

